{"ok":true,"data":{"kind":"command","command":"evidence add","summary":"Record one attributed EvidenceRecord for a task or scenario (promoted in the same run under `write: { promote: auto }` or with --promote; under `write.promote: manual`, commit it with `canon gate promote`)","effect":"write","idempotency":"content-keyed","effectNote":"refreshes stale scenario-index records once nothing refuses the call; a refused call writes nothing","options":[{"name":"task","valueName":"TASK_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*#[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)*$"},"help":"Plan task this evidence attests to (<change_id>#<n>); required unless --scenario is given"},{"name":"project","valueName":"PROJECT_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$"},"help":"Spec corpus id for --scenario (canon keys a scenario by the composite (project_id, scenario_id)). Must name a spec root configured in canon.yaml, or the add is refused (SPEC_ROOT_NOT_FOUND) before anything is written"},{"name":"class","defaultNote":"test-run when a --report is given","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\u0000]*\\P{White_Space}[^\u0000]*$"},"help":"What CLASS of evidence is attested to (test-run, review, ...); default `test-run` when a --report is given. `audit` is refused: an external evaluator's re-audit is `canon evidence audit`"},{"name":"ref","valueName":"TEXT","defaultNote":"the --report paths, comma-separated, when one is given","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\u0000]*\\P{White_Space}[^\u0000]*$"},"help":"The reference a reader can resolve: a command line, commit sha, or report path (default: the --report paths, comma-separated, when one is given). NEVER run or resolved by canon"},{"name":"verdict","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["faithful","not-applicable","divergent"],"defaultNote":"derived from the bound cases when a --report is given, else faithful","help":"faithful / not-applicable / divergent. Given a --report and no --verdict, the verdict is derived from the bound cases (any failed: divergent; a skipped case and none failed: not-applicable; else faithful), one record at a time with --all-scenarios; with no report the default is faithful. An explicit faithful over a failed or skipped case is refused"},{"name":"summary","valueName":"TEXT","domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"One line of text, with or without --task; a task's flipped row shows it as the latest summary (scanned for fabrication markers). The white space around it is trimmed; a control character or line break inside it is refused"},"command-result",{"name":"scenario","valueName":"SCENARIO_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9-]+\\.[a-z0-9-]+\\.[0-9]{2,}$"},"help":"Scenario this evidence also joins to"},"run",{"name":"surface-ref","valueName":"PATH_OR_EFFECT","repeatable":true,"domain":{"pattern":"^\\P{White_Space}([^\\n\\r\u0000]*\\P{White_Space})?$"},"help":"A path pattern from the repository root (src/, src/**) or effect:<kebab-slug>; persisted as surface_ref"},{"name":"actor","valueName":"ACTOR_ID","default":"canon","domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"The attesting actor's id (recorded as the attestation's author). One line of text: the white space around it is trimmed; a control character or line break inside it is refused"},{"name":"role","defaultNote":"the role declared with --as or CANON_ROLE","env":"CANON_ROLE","domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$"},"help":"The attesting role; `canon gate promote` derives its run_seq partition key from it. Default: the declared role (--as / CANON_ROLE); required when none is declared"},{"name":"session","valueName":"SESSION_ID","domain":{"pattern":"^[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}]([^\\p{Cc}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])?$"},"help":"The attesting session (recorded as actor.session_id). Under require_review.distinct_actor a review from this session does not count"},{"name":"approver","valueName":"NAME","domain":{"pattern":"^\\p{White_Space}*([^\\p{Cc}\\p{Zl}\\p{Zp}]*[^\\p{Cc}\\p{White_Space}])\\p{White_Space}*$"},"help":"Human approval identity; authentication comes only from the detached signature"},{"name":"approval-role","valueName":"ROLE","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["human"],"help":"Approval role; only human is eligible for risk approval"},{"name":"signature-file","valueName":"FILE","valueType":"path","help":"Armored SSH detached signature file. Canon never signs on the user's behalf"},{"name":"approval-at","valueName":"TIMESTAMP","domain":{"pattern":"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}[Tt][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(\\.[0-9]+)?([Zz]|[-+][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"},"help":"The approval time included in the signed approval payload: an RFC 3339 date-time (`<ts>`; a date alone is refused), the value the signature was made over"},"rev",{"name":"artifact","valueName":"PATH","valueType":"path","repeatable":true,"help":"EXPERIMENTAL: bind any file (trace, screenshots, agent QA log, report) by sha256; repeatable; must be inside the repo; with --all-scenarios only as <scenario-id>=<path>, bound to that scenario's record alone"},"report",{"name":"report-case","valueName":"NAME","repeatable":true,"help":"EXPERIMENTAL: also bind this report case (a Rust test: its function name); repeatable. Cases whose own scenario id is this one are always bound"},{"name":"all-scenarios","valueType":"switch","help":"One record per indexed scenario of --project that owns a case in the --report(s), all or nothing (see below)"},"max-artifact-mib","override-reason","promote","no-promote","repo","as"],"constraints":[{"rule":"atMostOne","names":["promote","no-promote"]},{"rule":"atLeastOne","names":["class","report"]},{"rule":"atLeastOne","names":["ref","report"]},{"rule":"atLeastOne","names":["task","scenario","all-scenarios"],"code":"EVIDENCE_REQUIRED","help":"A record needs a coverage subject: a task, a scenario, or one record per scenario of a report."},{"rule":"forbids","if":{"name":"all-scenarios"},"then":["scenario","task","report-case","approver","approval-role","signature-file","approval-at"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_CONFLICT","help":"--all-scenarios writes one record per scenario its report owns, so it names no single subject."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"all-scenarios"},"then":["report"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_REQUIRED","help":"--all-scenarios splits a --report by the scenario each case belongs to."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"report-case"},"then":["report"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_REQUIRED","help":"--report-case names a case of a --report."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"command-result"},"then":["summary"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_REQUIRED","help":"The captured output backs a --summary."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"approver"},"then":["approval-role","signature-file","approval-at"],"code":"EVIDENCE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","help":"The four approval options (`--approver`, `--approval-role`, `--signature-file`, `--approval-at`) go together: giving one needs the other three."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"approval-role"},"then":["approver","signature-file","approval-at"],"code":"EVIDENCE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","help":"The four approval options (`--approver`, `--approval-role`, `--signature-file`, `--approval-at`) go together: giving one needs the other three."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"signature-file"},"then":["approver","approval-role","approval-at"],"code":"EVIDENCE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","help":"The four approval options (`--approver`, `--approval-role`, `--signature-file`, `--approval-at`) go together: giving one needs the other three."},{"rule":"requires","if":{"name":"approval-at"},"then":["approver","approval-role","signature-file"],"code":"EVIDENCE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","help":"The four approval options (`--approver`, `--approval-role`, `--signature-file`, `--approval-at`) go together: giving one needs the other three."}],"validators":[{"arguments":["approval-at"],"code":"USAGE","description":"Reads the value as an RFC 3339 date-time (`<ts>`), the instant signed into the payload; the date and the time must exist on the calendar and the clock: `<ts>` and `<ts>` are refused."},{"arguments":["surface-ref"],"code":"USAGE","description":"A risk surface is `effect:<kebab-slug>` (lowercase letters and digits in hyphen-separated parts) or a repository-relative path: not absolute and with no `..` component."},{"arguments":["class"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_INVALID","description":"`--class audit` is refused: an external evaluator's re-audit is `canon evidence audit`."},{"arguments":["artifact","scenario","all-scenarios"],"code":"EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_CONFLICT","description":"An `--artifact` binds to one record. Without `--all-scenarios` a scoped `--artifact <scenario-id>=<path>` must name the record's own `--scenario`; with `--all-scenarios` every `--artifact` must be scoped (a bare path would bind to every record of the batch). The part before the first `=` is a scope only when it is shaped like a scenario id."}],"errors":["ARTIFACTS_DIGEST_INVALID","ARTIFACTS_STORE_DENIED","ARTIFACTS_STORE_INVALID","ARTIFACTS_STORE_REQUIRED","ARTIFACTS_STORE_UNAVAILABLE","BRIEF_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","BRIEF_APPROVAL_STALE","BRIEF_MIGRATION_REQUIRED","COMMIT_REQUIRED","CONFIG_DENIED","CONFIG_INVALID","CONFIG_REQUIRED","CONFIG_UNAVAILABLE","EVIDENCE_ARGUMENT_CONFLICT","EVIDENCE_BINDING_DENIED","EVIDENCE_BINDING_INVALID","EVIDENCE_BINDING_NOT_FOUND","EVIDENCE_BINDING_UNAVAILABLE","EVIDENCE_CONTRACT_CONFLICT","EVIDENCE_INCOMPLETE","EVIDENCE_NOTE_INVALID","EVIDENCE_REPORT_CONFLICT","EVIDENCE_STALE","LAYOUT_MIGRATION_REQUIRED","PLAN_CORPUS_DENIED","PLAN_CORPUS_INVALID","PLAN_CORPUS_UNAVAILABLE","PLAN_SOURCES_REQUIRED","PROMOTION_FAILED","PROMOTION_INVALID","REPO_DENIED","REPO_INVALID","REPO_LOCK_UNAVAILABLE","REPO_UNAVAILABLE","ROLE_INVALID","SPEC_ROOT_NOT_FOUND","SUBJECT_APPROVAL_REQUIRED","SUBJECT_INVALID","TASK_EVIDENCE_INVALID","TASK_NOT_FOUND","TYPED_ATOMS_INVALID","WRITE_DENIED","WRITE_FAILED","WRITE_INVALID"],"outputs":[{"schemaRef":"#/schemas/EvidenceAddReport","schemaVersion":"1.1"},{"schemaRef":"#/schemas/BatchEvidenceAddReport","schemaVersion":"1.1","batch":true,"when":"--input is an array or NDJSON"}],"input":{"argumentsRef":"#/schemas/EvidenceAddArguments","batch":true,"maxBytes":8388608,"maxItems":10000,"example":{"class":"test-run","ref":"npm test","role":"implementer","scenario":"auth.login.01"}},"examples":["canon evidence add --scenario auth.login.01 --class test-run --ref \"npm test\" --role implementer --json"],"x-canon":{"roles":["implementer"]}},"meta":{"command":"schema","schemaVersion":"1.5","tool":"canon","toolVersion":"0.39.1","contract":"atip/1","contractVersion":"1.5"}}
